<title>USA: Mass. Pilgrim 1 nuclear plant shuts for refueling.</title>
<headline>Mass. Pilgrim 1 nuclear plant shuts for refueling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 670 megawatt Pilgrim 1 nuclear power plant in Plymouth, Mass., was shut, as expected, late Friday for scheduled refueling and maintenance, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>In Monday's daily status report, NRC provided a restart date of April 9 for Pilgrim 1.</p>
<p>Boston Edison Co is the operator and sole owner of Pilgrim 1.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
